// Specialised: the economy.

:: anchor=left size=20 pad=26 enter=type speed=44 line=1.4

@Signals Officer
:: point=tab.economy gate=1 until=open:economy
The economy -- open it. Everything else in the game is an argument about how to spend
what this produces.
---
@Signals Officer
§**Industry**§ grows where people already are. A factory in an empty province
is an expensive shed -- the population is the input, not the building.
---
@Signals Officer
Income arrives once a turn, on the turn. Commit to more than you have and the
shortfall does not politely wait: it comes out of readiness, and you find out
about it in a battle.
---
@Signals Officer
:: point=panel.close gate=1 until=closed:economy
Out again, and we will look at a single province instead.
---
@Signals Officer
:: point=panel.province until=selected:any
Click one of ours. Per province, the panel shows what it produces and what it
holds. Resources are worth more processed than dug up, so an industrial
province beside a rich one is worth more than either alone.
---
@Signals Officer
And policies are a §**standing bill**§, not a purchase. Every one you run is
subtracted every turn, forever, whether or not it is still doing anything.

That is the economy. Anything else?
